WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.640
When President Biden announced his vaccine mandate&nbsp;
plan in September, Gallup reported that roughly six

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:15.920
in ten adults favored the requirements for federal&nbsp;
government workers, employees of large companies,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.680
and workers at hospitals. 58% of employed people&nbsp;
in Gallup's September polling supported their

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.920
employer requiring employees without a medical&nbsp;
exemption to get the jab, while 36% were opposed.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:34.640
In an early October Axios/Ipsos poll, 27% said&nbsp;
their employer was requiring them to get one,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.400
up from 16% in August. Americans believe their&nbsp;
fellow citizens should make the choice themselves

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:46.800
about getting a vaccine. An August USA Today/Ipsos&nbsp;
poll found that 72% percent of Americans agreed

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.800
that people have a right not to get the vaccine.&nbsp;
At the same time, 70% said that unvaccinated people

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.800
should not expect to be around vaccinated people.&nbsp;
65% said the unvaccinated should be barred from

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.320
large events, and separately, from traveling by&nbsp;
plane. At this time, most Americans don't see the

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.182
vaccine as an infringement on personal liberty.

00:01:08.182 --> 00:01:13.250
Do you think Americans should be required to get the covid vaccine? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.656
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:17.656 --> 00:01:22.480
and be sure to like and&nbsp;subscribe
for more research and videos from AEI.

